.Dd November 20, 2026
.Dt SAMPLE 1
.Os Minkar
.Sh NAME
.Nm sample
.Nd show where a running process spends its time
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Ar pid | name
.Op Ar duration Op Ar interval
.Op Fl file Ar path
.Op Fl mayDie
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
stops the process again and again for
.Ar duration
seconds (10 by default), every
.Ar interval
milliseconds (1 by default), and takes the stack of each of its threads by
following their frame pointers.
It then prints, for each thread, a call tree with how many samples each
frame was in, the frames most often at the top of a stack, and the images
the process has loaded.
Frames are named from the symbol tables of those images.
.Pp
A process given by name must be the only one whose name contains it.
Examining another user's process needs root.
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Fl file Ar path
Write the analysis to
.Ar path
instead of the standard output.
.It Fl mayDie
Say nothing if the process exits before the sampling ends.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr leaks 1 ,
.Xr dtrace 1
.Sh BUGS
Frames of code built without frame pointers are missed.
